# Story 61: Tool Approval Flow (50s)
# Hook: Your AI agent never touches a file or runs a destructive command without your say-so.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-061-tool-approval-flow.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Your AI agent never touches a file or runs a destructive command without your say-so.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh. We are in shell mode -- your familiar terminal.

[00:08.0 --> 00:16.0]
Double-press Escape for prompt mode, then ask the agent to change a file. Tools like file_edit always need approval.

[00:16.0 --> 00:30.0]
Before anything is written, the footer shows the action and a diff preview. Nothing changes until you decide.

[00:30.0 --> 00:40.0]
Press y to approve. The edit applies and the agent continues. Press n to reject and the action is cancelled.

[00:40.0 --> 00:47.0]
Reads and searches run freely. But writes, patches, commits, and dangerous bash are all gated behind you.

[00:47.0 --> 00:50.0]
You are always the final approver.

